{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>Budgets need teeth, and they need a way to be raised on purpose</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      A budget check that can be silently skipped or overridden by anyone at any time isn't much better than no check, treat crossing the line the same way you'd treat a failing test: fix the size, or make a deliberate, reviewed decision to raise the number.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Track more than one bundle if your app ships more than one meaningful entry point, a single "main.js" number hides regressions in a lazy-loaded route or a vendor chunk that users on that specific page still have to download.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Prefer a tool that reports gzip or brotli size, not raw bytes, since that's what actually crosses the network, and set the limit against the compressed size your CDN actually serves, a budget measured on the wrong number gives you false confidence either direction.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

