{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A bundle-size limit that only lives in a doc gets silently violated, because nothing actually checks it on every change.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">A CI tool like size-limit or bundlesize turns the budget into a build step that fails the PR the moment it's crossed, with the exact size delta visible right there.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Track every meaningful entry point on compressed (gzip/brotli) size, and require a deliberate, reviewed change to the budget file itself to raise the limit — never a silent one.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
